TB710FU macOS 27.3: run nmb_device_open and pipeline creation on a 16 MiB stack
when called from a thread with less than 2 MiB of stack (e.g. WindowServer's
512 KiB pthread_create secondary thread).

Hardware evidence (pl85 com5_pl85_live.log, pl86 com5_pl86_live.log):
- WindowServer calls MTLCopyAllDevices -> NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin ->
  native_bridge_metal_open -> nmb_device_open -> Device::system_default_with on
  a 512 KiB pthread_create thread.
- Rust's inline stack probe at NativeAdrenoMetal+0xe809b8 (352 KiB frame, total
  stack depth 515.6 KiB > 512 KiB) hits the 4 KiB VM_PROT_NONE stack guard page
  and terminates WindowServer with SIGBUS (status=0xa, reason 2:10).
- onSufficientStack runs inline with zero overhead on >=2 MiB stacks and uses
  the existing 16 MiB onLargeStack helper on smaller secondary threads.

diff --git a/drivers/AdrenoMetal/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm b/drivers/AdrenoMetal/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
--- a/drivers/AdrenoMetal/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
+++ b/drivers/AdrenoMetal/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
@@ -666,6 +666,10 @@
  pthread_attr_destroy(&attr);
  if(made)pthread_join(thread,nullptr);else body();
 }
+static void onSufficientStack(void (^body)(void)) {
+ if(pthread_get_stacksize_np(pthread_self())>=(2u<<20)){body();return;}
+ onLargeStack(body);
+}
